  "details": "<p>A multidisciplinary team of researchers, headquartered at Emory University, have produced an extensive and growing website about the sanctuary. It includes background information, 3D walk-throughs, reconstructions and bibliography:</p>\r\n<div>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Susan Blevins, Bonna Wescoat, and Elizabeth Hornor (eds.), <em>Samothrace: Framing the Mysteries in the Sanctuary of the Great Gods:</em> <a href=\"http://www.samothrace.emory.edu/\" title=\"Samothrace: Framing the Mysteries in the Sanctuary of the Great Gods\">www.samothrace.emory.edu</a>.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The \"Sanctuary of the great gods\" on the island of Samothrace, one of the chief Panhellenic sanctuaries of the ancient Greek world.",
